1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,992
My heart stopped beating three minutes ago, and yet, here I am, waking up inside a freezing glass tube.

2
00:00:08,292 --> 00:00:17,628
The emergency lights pulse red, casting harsh shadows across the sterile walls of the underground activation chamber I call home.

3
00:00:17,928 --> 00:00:25,920
A digital screen flashes my exact serial number. I am not a person. I am a reserve body, waiting for a crash.

4
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:34,308
Every memory in my head belongs to him. The coffee shops, the heartbreaks, the laughs. They were all just downloaded.

5
00:00:34,608 --> 00:00:42,384
My primary self was supposed to survive his mountain climb today. That is the only reason my pod was programmed to open.

6
00:00:42,684 --> 00:00:50,916
I press my palm against the heavy steel exit door, expecting it to remain locked until the system syncs our lives.

7
00:00:51,216 --> 00:00:59,352
The door slides open with a hiss, spilling golden morning sunlight onto my bare feet for the very first time.

8
00:00:59,652 --> 00:01:07,644
I step out onto the quiet forest trail, ready to finally take over his life and live freely under the sun.

9
00:01:07,944 --> 00:01:17,616
Then my wrist implant buzzes. A red notification reads: Primary signal lost permanently. Signal flatline confirmed at dawn.

10
00:01:17,916 --> 00:01:23,556
If the original is truly gone forever, then who exactly am I backing up now?
